{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1223547-chases-with-multiple-character","id":1223547,"title":"Chases with multiple character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-31T01:31:36-07:00","id":1223547,"title":"Chases with multiple character","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I really like the way to deal with chases the CoD propose, but I have some doubt when the pursuers / fugitives are more than one.<br /> <br /> I.e. 3 wolves are pursuing 2 PC, how should I deal with this? Should anyone have its own target number to achieve it's goal? <br /> If one of the pursuers achieve it's goal, which one of the 2 characters is reached? The one with the lowest number of successes achieved? But in this case, since the target number is built comparing the modifier table against a specific target, should I decide before which pursuer is pursuing which target?<br /> <br /> It doesn't seems very light to me with several character involved. Any suggestion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T02:42:06-07:00","id":1223556,"title":"","content":"The easiest way to handle it (relatively) is to make it a teamwork action. Pick a primary actor for each side, the non-primaries all roll, and the primaries get their successes (or possibly penalized if someone dramatically fails) as bonus dice. Use the Primaries for setting the TNs (and switching Primaries might change the TN too, also keep in mind for the Edge possibly switching if the new Primary might have an advantage as the Chase scenario changes).<br /> <br /> If the ones being pursued split up, it's probably best to run two (or more) Chases even if that can get a bit chaotic.<br /> <br /> This approach <b>heavily</b> favors the team with the most characters, but that's not inherently a bad thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T04:02:47-07:00","id":1223566,"title":"","content":"It was something I was thought about and I like it. <br /> Furthermore the fact that team with more character would be advantaged is something that I agree and, actually, very reasonable (up to a certain limit of characters)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 05-31-2018, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}